# a-crew-that-clears-up — plan 13 V2, and the answer to plan 12 B7.
#
# `a-tower-buries-its-own-wall.keys` plus ONE line: `park 7 0`.
# Everything else is identical — same ground, same core, same wall,
# same tower, same waves.
#
#   undefended:                     61 ticks   ( 41 s)
#   sealed wall:                   104 ticks   ( 69 s)
#   sealed wall + tower:            95 ticks   ( 63 s)   the tower LOSES
#   this file — and a crew:        121 ticks   ( 81 s)   the tower PAYS
#
# ⚠⚠ **This is where the tower stops being a liability.**  B7 measured
# a base that fell SOONER for having a gun on it: the tower killed
# eight robots at the foot of its own wall, three of them fell on
# (6, 0), and 1.5 m of dead is inside plan 12 B0's [1.0, 2.0] ramp band
# onto a 3.0 m wall — so the survivors climbed over a wall that never
# lost a tenth of its HP.  One vehicle standing in the kill zone takes
# that ramp away as fast as the tower builds it, and the attackers are
# put back onto the wall.
#
# ⚠ **The wall's HP is the evidence, not the clock.**  Without a crew
# the wall ends at 96.7 of 100 — barely scratched, because nobody had
# to break it.  With one it ends at 69.3, because the only way in was
# through.  The clock is the consequence; the HP is the mechanism.
#
# ── ⚠ The crew is OUTSIDE, and that is this scenario's caveat ────
#
# `park 7 0` puts the vehicle beyond its own perimeter, and it has to
# be there: the ramp forms where the enemies die, which is outside the
# wall, and a hover unit climbs 0.4 m against a 3.0 m wall.  **A sealed
# base locks its own crew in.**
#
# So this file is a player who chose to stay out in the open — legal,
# and exactly the trade `DESIGN.md` § What kind of game this is
# describes: *"a kill zone that keeps working — bodies pile into a
# ramp, so someone must drive INTO it and clear them"*.  What it is
# NOT is a player who can pop out and come back, and that needs
# `hover_clearance_boost` (3.0 m, exactly a wall) — plan 13 V4.  Until
# then, clearing a sealed base's kill zone is a one-way commitment.
#
# ⚠ And nothing can hurt the vehicle yet: § 8's blocker-damage model is
# not built (`plans/13` § What this plan does NOT build), so standing
# in a kill zone is currently free.  It is not meant to be.

echo a crew that clears up: one vehicle, and the tower finally pays

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

# The tower, one hex behind the wall it covers (plan 12 B5b).
do cycle_kind
click 3 0
marker 3 0 tower

do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 3 3
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -3 -2 12 -2
drag -3 -1 12 -1
drag -3 0 12 0
drag -3 1 12 1
drag -3 2 12 2
count painted 80 80

palette 9
click 5 -2
click 5 -1
click 5 0
click 5 1
click 5 2
kind 5 0 wall
hp 5 0 100.0 100.0

# The crew: parked in the kill zone, one hex clear of where the bodies
# will fall.  It clears whatever rubble it is standing on or beside, at
# `numbers.json` § player_vehicle.salvage_rate — one dead robot a
# second — with no key pressed, because clearing is a POSITION
# (`DESIGN.md` § 11).
park 7 0
vehicle 7 0

wave 5
count alive 5 5
wallet 200.0 200.0

tick 22
wave 8

# ⚠ **Eleven, where the same base without a crew reads nine** — the
# tower is two kills BEHIND at this point, not ahead.  Clearing the
# heap changes where the survivors stand, and a robot that is not where
# the gun is looking does not get shot.  It catches up: both bases end
# on five alive, so the crew's whole contribution is timing and terrain
# rather than damage.
count alive 11 11

fall 800
ticks 116 126
wallet 0.0 0.0

# ── What the crew changed ───────────────────────────────────────

# No ramp.  The tower built one all through the run and the crew ate it
# as fast as it appeared.
pile 6 0 0.0 0.0

# So they had to come through the wall instead — a third of it gone,
# against the 3.3 HP the same wall lost with nobody clearing up.
kind 5 0 wall
hp 5 0 65.0 75.0

# The tower's own tally is unchanged: eight of thirteen, the same
# 30-shot budget.  ⚠ That is the point — **the crew added no damage
# whatsoever.**  Every extra second this base survived came from
# denying the attackers a staircase, which is a mechanic with no
# numbers of its own.
count alive 5 5

snap b7_a_crew_that_clears_up
